<p>The location of the job plays a significant role in the figure of your salary. The areas dealing with the west, such as Pune and Bangalore, offer higher salaries than the others. The Delhi-National Capital Region (NCR) area also has a fair pay scale. The farther north you move, the lower is the pay scale.</p>
<p>For example, your pay scale at Delhi (NCR) is Rs. 55,000 per month. But now that you have to move back to your hometown in Jaipur, the pay scale available there is Rs. 35,000 per month. Here, nothing has changed; your job profile or the company, and you also have more experience than you had when you started off as a business analyst. But the location factor is prominent, and hence the change of figure in salary. </p>
<p><em>Therefore, while these figures can be used as a comparative, they must not be used as an absolute.</em></p>
<h2>Business Analyst Skills</h2>
<p>Structural changes and innovation administration are an integral part of <strong>business analyst skills</strong>. The insights an analyst provides play a crucial role in defining or reengineering the functions of an organization. Below is a list of the top five critical skills required to become a prominent business analyst in the business analytics realm:</p>
<h3><strong>Business Pivotal Thinking</strong></h3>
<p>Since the archaic period, critical thinking has been a point of discussion. The Greek philosophers Plato and Socrates have also provided the world with insightful books showing the foremost importance of critical thinking. To think logically about an idea or a situation is what is expected from a business analyst. As his one wrong move can cause the business huge loss in terms of money, performance, appearance, and goodwill. Among the very important business analyst job responsibilities is to examine critical thinking elements; hindsight, and foresight effectively. </p>
<h3><strong>Organizational Problem Solving Skills</strong></h3>
<p>Hindrances are indispensable in the business world. However, in the words of <em>Gary Vaynerchuk, “who fears failures cannot experience success.”</em> From Forbes to The Wall Street Journal, Gary is known for his problem-solving skills.</p>
<p>By just posting his videos on wine ( his family’s business), later on, helped him become a wine critic. And now he is an entrepreneur, motivational speaker, author, digital marketing expert, and vlogger. He had a problem with reaching maximum people and letting them know about his family’s business. His solution to this problem was simple yet extremely effective – he posted videos regularly without putting any thought to the quality of both the video and content. His consistency was the solution ‘key’ he needed for his problem.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/image-4-22-1-600x500.jpg" alt="">
<em>Source: <a href="https://www.booksmartr.com/summary/-askgaryvee">https://www.booksmartr.com/summary/-askgaryvee</a></em></p>
<h3><strong>Computer Skills</strong></h3>
<p>As stated above, documentation of the findings is a fundamental skill. Therefore, to put the information in graphical and statistical form, acquiring computer knowledge is a must. Also, for an <strong>entry-level business analyst</strong> conducting research related to market, trends, consumer behavior, competitors techniques is a prerequisite. Therefore, understanding the basics of computers is mandatory to apply for this job. From Microsoft Word to PowerPoint to MS Excel a business analyst must know these tools through and through.</p>
<h3><strong>Analytics Skills</strong></h3>
<p>This is the first skill that a <strong>Business Analyst Role description</strong> demands. There is a fine line difference between critical thinking skills and analytical skills. Critical thinking is based on logical reasoning and the latter decides the judgment founded on this logical reasoning element. These skills include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Cost analysis</li>
<li>Predictive analysis</li>
<li>Industry analysis</li>
<li>Process analysis</li>
<li>Inventory analysis</li>
<li>Leadership analysis</li>
<li>Consumer behavior analysis</li>
<li>Risk analysis</li>
</ul>
<h3><strong>The Art of Communicating Effectively</strong></h3>
<p>Undoubtedly, communication acts as a strong thread between the listener and the speaker. A business analyst must have interpersonal skills – knows the ideology behind communicating with empathy and not sympathy, authoritative, and yet keeping the tone subtle. Indeed, the magic of words helps companies close clients, influence customers to try a product, and convince management of a change needed in leadership. The book ‘How to Have Confidence and Power in Dealing with People’ authored by <a href="https://www.amazon.com/s/ref=dp_byline_sr_book_1?ie=UTF8&#x26;field-author=Leslie+T.+Giblin&#x26;text=Leslie+T.+Giblin&#x26;sort=relevancerank&#x26;search-alias=books">Leslie T. Giblin</a> showcases why mastering and perusing communication skills is vital in both, life and work.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/image-5-20-1-600x500.jpg" alt=""></p>
<p><strong><em>According to a</em></strong> <a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/bernardmarr/2019/10/28/the-10-most-important-job-skills-every-company-will-be-looking-for-in-2020/#2b436eb167b6"><strong><em>Forbes article</em></strong></a><strong><em>, “three out of these five skills are identified as the most required skills in the year 2020 by the World Economic Forum. “</em></strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong><em>You may also like to read: <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/the-pre-requisites-of-business-analytics/">Prerequisites of Business Analytics</a></em></strong></p>
</blockquote>
<h2><strong>Business Analyst Certifications &#x26; Courses</strong></h2>
<p>Earning a certificate in a particular field boosts the confidence alone and gives the leverage of earning better. As a business analyst is an emerging opportunity in the business world, it is crucial to give your dreams the wings to behold it – <em>certification</em>. <strong>Business Analyst certifications</strong> are a strong medium for materializing whatever one has understood while intensely studying this domain.  Below is a list of the top <strong>5 Business Analyst Certifications for a career in Analytics</strong>:</p>
<p>1. <strong>Analytics Edge – AnalytixLabs</strong></p>
<p>This <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/business-analyst-training-course-online">business analytics certification course</a> is best suitable for beginners looking a short-term course that covers all the essential skills required to kick start the career as a Data Analyst or Business Analyst. This program spans over 3-4 months to <strong>cover hands-on analytics skills on most widely used tools such as MS-Excel, SQL, Tableau &#x26; R. Available in all 3 modes of learning i.e. Classroom, Interactive Live Online and eLearning.</strong></p>
<p>2. <strong>Business Analytics 360 – AnalytixLabs</strong></p>
<p>One of the most coveted courses offered by AnalytixLabs and rated as one of the <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/business-analytics-data-science-course">top Business Analytics course in India</a>. This extensive program spans over 6 months and with the flexibility to complete the certification in 12 months. This training program begins with basic data analytics &#x26; reporting skills, and graduates to more advanced modules such as statistical analysis and machine learning modeling.  <strong>Available in all 3 modes of learning i.e. Classroom, Interactive Live Online, and eLearning.</strong></p>
<p>3. <strong>Columbia’s MicroMasters program in Business Analytics</strong></p>
<p>This is an online series of courses and each course is followed by a final exam week. The curriculum is designed to provide learners with a series of courses that emphasize the use of statistical analysis, computing tools, and analytics models to predict the outcomes of various business decisions and identify the best implementation.</p>
<p>4. <strong><a href="https://www.stern.nyu.edu/programs-admissions/ms-business-analytics">Master of Science in Business Analytics</a> – NYU Stern</strong></p>
<p>This is a <a href="https://www.stern.nyu.edu/programs-admissions/ms-business-analytics">full-time Business Analytics master program</a> offered by New York University and suited for experienced professionals. Aimed to drive better business results by gaining the ability to transform data into a powerful and predictive strategic asset. Participants of this program will have exposure to methodologies that support data-driven decision making.</p>
<p>5. <strong>Management Program in Business Analytics – ISB</strong></p>
<p>The <a href="https://www.isb.edu/lp/cee/ampba/">AMPBA</a> has been designed for working professionals at any career stage from across industries, looking to transform data into actionable insights. The program will especially benefit executives who are Data science enthusiasts and IT professionals.</p>
<h3><strong>Business Analytics Tools</strong></h3>
<p>Here is a list of some known Business Analytics Tools that can help in reporting, sleuth analysis, hindsight and foresight modeling, and studying big data:</p>
<ul>
<li>MS Excel</li>
<li>Structured Query Language (SQL)</li>
<li>R/ Python</li>
<li>Tableau</li>
<li>Qlikview</li>
<li>PowerBI</li>
<li>SAS</li>
<li>Statistical Package for the Social Sciences (SPSS)</li>
<li>Minitab</li>
</ul>
<h3><strong>Benefits of Business Analytics Tools:</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>Seamless tracking of business operations leads to quick, effective, and timely management of an organization’s processes.</li>
<li>These provide leverage over your competitors by aiding in knowing the market trends and consumer behavior better.</li>
<li>These aid in predicting future uncertainty and changing the marketing and business approach accordingly without hindering the daily operations of a business.</li>
<li>A statistical representation of data aids an organization to comprehend which strategies went wrong where and how can these be rectified.</li>
<li>These aid in calculating the KPIs of an organization for creating effective decision-making strategies for the future.</li>
</ul>
<h2><strong>Concluding Thoughts</strong></h2>
<p>In today’s times, a business analyst is an essential cog of the business world. From being resourceful to implementing the decisions, he carries a burden of making the business known to the world by eliminating the barriers to compelling business strategies. As the world is seeing an escalation in the demand of BA experts, to add a feather in your career cap, Analytixlabs is providing an opportunity to various participants to piecemeal explore this realm and obtain a valuable course certificate in the end.  </p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong><em>You may also like to read: <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/the-complete-guide-to-starting-your-career-as-a-business-analyst-in-india/">The Complete Guide to Start Your Career as a Business Analyst in India</a></em></strong></p>
</blockquote>
', 'Business Analyst', ARRAY['Business Analyst', 'Business Analytics']::text[], 'Beginner', '11 min read', 'al-editorial', 'https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/image-1-38-1-3.jpg', 'What Does a Business Analyst Do? Responsibilities, Roles & Salary', 'Published', '2020-07-08T08:24:58.000Z'::timestamptz, '2020-07-08T08:24:58.000Z'::timestamptz, '{"canonicalUrl":"https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/business-analyst-roles-and-responsibilities/","noIndex":true,"metaTitle":"What Does a Business Analyst Do? Responsibilities, Roles & Salary","metaDesc":"To know more about what a Business Analyst does and what are his roles & responsibilities. This article will take you through the Job Description, Salary, Skills & other aspects of a Business Analyst."}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '', '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"entityTags":["Business Analyst","Business Analytics","general"],"enabled":true}'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"qa":true,"faqSchema":true,"moderation":"auto"}'::jsonb, '{"showLeadGen":false,"showNextSteps":false,"showCourseCta":false,"showRightSidebar":true}'::jsonb),
('What Business Analyst Skills You Need to Master for Fast-Track Career', 'business-analyst-skills-need-master-fast-track-career', 'Choosing a career as a Business Analyst means you have to constantly deal with all the new tools and technologies arriving in the data science market. With a', '<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/Blog1-FB-March-300x300.jpg" alt="">Choosing a career as a Business Analyst means you have to constantly deal with all the new tools and technologies arriving in the data science market. With a creative and flexible bent of mind, a good business analyst can become hugely productive and successful in a dynamic environment. Of course, this requires careful selection of Business Analyst (BA) training that would help any professional fully understand the real opportunities and challenges available.</p>
<p>Here are the top business analyst technical skills and non-tech requirements to succeed in the highly competitive Business Intelligence and Analysis market.</p>
<h2><strong>Business Analyst Technical Skills</strong></h2>
<p>Business analysis is a hardcore technology-driven part of any organization.</p>
<p>Business Analyst technical skills are the hard skills required to perform the key functions of a business analyst. In any <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/business-analyst-training-course-online">business analyst training</a>, professionals are trained with various scientific tools and auditing platforms to derive as much information as possible from limited data.</p>
<p>A major function for any Business Analyst pertains to building a powerful technology stack of business applications based on IT and data governance regulations.</p>
<p>In the context of Business Analysis and Intelligence roles, these are the most essential practices you have to master.</p>
<p>A productive business analyst preparation course would train professionals in these core skill areas –</p>
<p>–       Effective Collaboration with Business Applications</p>
<p>–       Understanding the role and effect of Enterprise Architecture in business productivity</p>
<p>–       Measuring the performance of teams and verticals using life cycle management analytics and business analyst tools</p>
<h2><strong>Powerful Communication and Persuasion Skills</strong></h2>
<p>Apart from the important business analyst technical skills, the Business Analysts are required to persuade the IT and Product Development teams for every project. The testing team generally works in close quarters with the BA team, analyzing whether they meet the quality testing and assurance standards in the shortest lead time.</p>
<p>Good communication skills, regardless of the mode of messaging, help clear the ambiguity in the initial phases of any project.</p>
<p>A BA team would deal with thousands of emails, internally and externally, to get the correct information from the vendors, stakeholders, investors and budgeting team. This leads to establishing accuracy in finance and investment details that could be later shared with all the stakeholders without any ambiguity.</p>
<h2><strong>Working with Excel, Outlook and Workflow Automation Tools</strong></h2>
<p>As a BA, professionals have to create a powerful workflow process that saves time, delivers results and is verifiable for results every quarter. This means you have to polish your skills in Microsoft Excel, Outlook, and a bunch of other software bundles for email.</p>
<p>To manage one-to-one, one-to-many, and many-to-one relationships, a BA must demonstrate a visible inclination to create logical process flows. Best requirement analysis tools help to build a clear business scenario to identify and map every relation with easy navigation.</p>
<p>Collaboration tools, including the ones provided with Microsoft 365, RingCentral, Wrike and others ensure better integration and work management in real time.</p>
<h2><strong>The Next Frontier: Data Visualization</strong></h2>
<p>In Business Analyst roles, a professional would deal with Big Data from various sources, including the Website, social media and mobile. In such cases, data visualization powered by AI would be the key skill to master.</p>
', 'Business Analyst', ARRAY['Business Analyst']::text[], 'Beginner', '2 min read', 'al-editorial', 'https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/Blog1-FB-March-300x300.jpg', 'What Business Analyst Skills You Need to Master for Fast-Track Career', 'Published', '2019-05-20T04:39:03.000Z'::timestamptz, '2019-05-20T04:39:03.000Z'::timestamptz, '{"canonicalUrl":"https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/business-analyst-skills-need-master-fast-track-career/","noIndex":true,"metaTitle":"What Business Analyst Skills You Need to Master for Fast-Track Career","metaDesc":"Choosing a career as a Business Analyst means you have to constantly deal with all the new tools and technologies arriving in the data science market. With a"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '', '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"entityTags":["Business Analyst","general"],"enabled":true}'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"qa":true,"faqSchema":true,"moderation":"auto"}'::jsonb, '{"showLeadGen":false,"showNextSteps":false,"showCourseCta":false,"showRightSidebar":true}'::jsonb),
('Data Analyst vs. Business Analyst - Which is for you?', 'business-analyst-vs-data-analyst', 'Many times the job titles of data analysts and business analysts are used interchangeably. Because both these analysts handle data, broadly speaking.', '<p>If this question is on your mind for some time, you’ve come to the right place.</p>
<p>Facts show that <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/what-is-data-analytics-complete-career-guide/"><strong>Data Analytics</strong></a> has always been a part of our workforce, consistently analyzing data and facts for companies. In smaller organizations, the job titles of data analysts and business analysts are often used interchangeably. This is mainly because both these analysts handle data (from a broader perspective). These roles are treated differently in large (or more mature) organizations. At times, the line of difference between data analyst and business analyst may be blurred, but, in the end, the job environment and what each does with the data differs.</p>
<p>Thanks to big data, data scientists across the globe came into the limelight. Their involvement with data within a company goes long and deep, making these scientists a core resource for any company.</p>
<h3>Why do companies value data (and data analysts)?</h3>
<p>The fact that companies are thriving on data is directly proportional to the high demand for data analyst role in company. Here, let’s talk about companies of enterprise stature.</p>
<p>These companies handle huge sets of data, both structured and unstructured. They need proper structuring and engineering brains to make sense of this huge data set. A data analyst analyses these data and creates measurable insights that are significant for any business to grow and thrive in such a competitive world.</p>
<p>Hence, it makes sense that companies value data and people who work with the same. These are the people who handle sensitive data and maintain privacy while deriving meaningful business insights from humongous data sets.</p>
<p>This analogy brings us to our next pertinent question: <strong>Should you opt for business analyst or data analyst profile?</strong></p>
<p>As I mentioned in the beginning, the difference between data analyst and business analyst lie in the area of work. In both the profiles, you will be dealing with data and trying to make sense of it; but your target and purpose will change with each profile.</p>
<p>To understand the similarities and difference between data analyst and business analyst, you need to understand what each profile is about clearly. When you want to pick a particular profile as your business analyst or data analyst role in company, you must understand where it will place you in the long run and if you are ready for it.</p>
<p>Let’s dig in!</p>
<h3>An Overview: Business Analyst vs Data Analyst</h3>
<p>A business analyst will always oversee the business implications of data on a larger scale. They predict long-term actions based on their research, for example, developing a new product line or prioritizing a business activity over others. This role requires a perfect amalgamation of applications, skill sets, and tools that will enable a business to measure business achievements and work on improving the effectiveness of any core business function, like marketing, sales, or IT.</p>
<p>On the other hand, a data analyst is responsible for determining patterns or trends by analyzing huge data sets. A data analyst predicts trends, concludes several hypotheses and enables a business to make data-driven decisions. When I say ‘hypotheses,’ it does not mean any random theory.</p>
<p>When a business appoints a data analyst, that analyst creates several hypotheses, like predicting certain business-driven conclusions, considering all the available resources and tentative business goals. After that, they analyze data, determine conclusions, and pit them against these hypotheses to see if they can be practically implemented. If yes, they pull out data-driven roadmaps to achieve them.</p>
<p>In layman’s terms, a data analyst can answer simple questions like the geographical impact of my mobile company or which customers will purchase in the next 30 days. This job role requires sufficient knowledge of a diverse set of approaches using statistical and machine techniques. The data analyst role in the company also has some overlap with the roles of a data scientist, data modeling engineer, and data mining specialist.</p>
<p>Summing it up, the role of business analyst and data analyst can be broken down into three sections: goals, data, and approach.</p>
<h4>Goals:</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Business analyst</strong>: To identify trends in an organization to conclude one version of the truth that can be optimized and used to improve business performance.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Data analyst</strong>: To recognize patterns in data and make accurate predictions considering all events of past, present, and probable future.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4>Data:</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Business analyst</strong>: Work with predefined data sources based on project goals.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Data analyst</strong>: Ad hoc work with data sources; data sources are added with time as correlations are discovered.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4>Approach:</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Business analyst</strong>: Defines goals and requisites for programs or projects.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Data analyst</strong>: Takes a predictive and prescriptive approach.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>This gives us a broader perspective on how business and data analysts approach or function within an organization. Now, let’s see what it requires to make a career as a business analyst and data analyst.</p>
<h3>Choosing Career Prospect: Business Analyst vs Data Analyst</h3>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/image-2-17-1-4.jpg" alt="Factors to decide your career"></p>
<p><strong>Educational background</strong></p>
<p>Blake Angove, <a href="https://www.thelasallenetwork.com/">LaSalle Network</a> (director of technology services), believes that business analyst and data analyst tend to come with different backgrounds both academically and professionally.</p>
<p>A business analyst usually will have completed an undergraduate degree in a major that is business-focused. This kind of qualification is considered ideal because a business analyst uses business requirements and works with the technical team to create a business feature or package.</p>
<p>A data analyst, on the other hand, works with large data sets to predict business outcomes. Hence, these professionals usually come with STEM majors with extensive mathematics, science, programming, databases, and predictive analytics.</p>
<p><strong>Interests</strong></p>
<p>This (and the next point) is very important to consider when trying to etch out a career path for yourself. Whatever role you pick should align with your interests. For instance, imagine a professional having interest in creating graphics for marketing but working with data! This is a classic example of resource waste. Don’t do that. If you find numbers and statistics interesting, you are more inclined to be a great data analyst. If your inclination is towards solving core business problems using data, then business analyst is the best role you can opt for.</p>
<p>A business analyst enjoys the corporate world and tends to solve business challenges on a larger scale. They are involved in researching, organizing, and looking into the implementation of a new workflow. Add to this, these professionals have amazing written and oral skills and are fantastic communicators. This is simply because business analysts are responsible for explaining their concepts to technical teams and stakeholders before a workflow is implemented practically.</p>
<p>On the contrary, a data analyst is driven by numbers. They excel in mathematics and statistics. These professionals look over data and extract meaningful insights from disparate sources and complex data points.</p>
<p><strong>Personal choice of career</strong></p>
<p>Your CHOICE is the most crucial factor in determining which role you will take. You might be great at communications, but your heart lies in the visual extraction of data. Try understanding where you actually want to be. Not just that, where do you see yourself in the next 5 years’ time after starting with either of the roles.</p>
<p>Your choice also depends on:</p>
<p>– Salary insights</p>
<p>– Your subject matters</p>
<p>Both these job roles may have different salaries or sometimes be the same as well. However, their potential career path will always differ. Take a look at how the career path for each of these roles looks:</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/image-3-15-1-600x500.jpg" alt="General career path for Data Analysts &#x26; Business Analysts"></p>
<p>Just know, you can pick any of the two roles, but it is always advisable to pick the one for which you can acquire the requisite skills.</p>
<p>You can look at the course materials on AnalytixLabs for each of these subject matters to get a better insight.</p>
<h3>Data Analyst vs Business Analyst Salary in India</h3>
<p>It’d be a lie to say salary isn’t important. It is very much important, but of course never at the cost of exploiting your talents.</p>
<p>Business analyst and data analyst can make amazing fortunes if they have the requisite skills and a determination to make it big.</p>
<p>Recent trends show that companies are more and more realizing the benefit of having an in-house business analyst. With a predicted growth rate of 19 percent in the next ten years, the role of a business analyst is expanding in terms of salary.</p>
<p>For instance, Glassdoor estimates the average salary for a business analyst to be about <a href="https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Salaries/new-york-city-business-analyst-salary-SRCH_IL.0,13_IM615_KO14,30.htm">$75,637</a>. Business Analyst Salary in India starts from about 3.5 lakhs and goes up to 15 lakhs per annum, with an average base of 7 lakhs per annum.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/image-6-3-1-3.jpg" alt="Business Analyst Salaries in India"></p>
<p>Similarly, Glassdoor estimates the salary of a data analyst in NYC to be about <a href="https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Salaries/new-york-city-data-analyst-salary-SRCH_IL.0,13_IM615_KO14,26.htm">$66,859</a>. In India, Data Analyst Salary starts from about 3 lakhs and goes up to 10 lakhs per annum, with an average base of 5 lakhs per annum.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/image-7-1-3.jpg" alt="Data Analyst Salaries in India"></p>
<p><strong>Important Tip:</strong> Initial salaries may be more appealing for the Business Analyst role. However, Data Analysts offers a promising gateway to more lucrative roles like Data Scientist, which is a more rewarding career choice than mid to long term.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong><em>You may also like to read out our latest post on <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/data-analyst-salary-in-india/">Data Analyst Salary in India</a></em></strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>This leads us to the next section:</strong></p>
<h4>What are the skills required: Business Analyst vs Data Analyst</h4>
<p>According to <a href="https://www.pwc.com/us/en/library/data-science-and-analytics.html">PWC</a>, you can see below the data skill sets you’ll require for data-related job roles.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/image-4-5-1-3.jpg" alt="Analytics &#x26; Data Science Job Skills"></p>
<p>We looked at various job postings on Glassdoor and noted the skill sets each role requires.</p>
<p>To be a business analyst, the most common skills required are:</p>
<ul>
<li>Data analysis and extensive data research</li>
<li>Detailed analytical capabilities</li>
<li>Quantitative mindset and business intelligence</li>
<li>Self-learner, investigative nature</li>
<li>SQL proficiency</li>
<li>Tableau experience</li>
<li>MS Excel, Word and PowerPoint skills</li>
<li>Strong verbal and written skills</li>
<li>Knowledge of statistical tool like R is an advantage</li>
</ul>
<p>For instance, here is a job posting for a business analyst at a New York-based venture capital and private equity company:</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/image-5-4-1-3.jpg" alt="Business Analyst Job Skills"></p>
<p>To be a data analyst, the most common skills required are:</p>
<ul>
<li>SQL, R, and Python</li>
<li>Advanced Microsoft Excel and Office skills</li>
<li>Analytical skills</li>
<li>Curiosity and reporting acumen</li>
<li>Understands data mining techniques</li>
<li>Familiarity with MapReduce, Spark, large-scale data frameworks, machine learning</li>
<li>Can juggle multiple projects</li>
<li>Strong verbal and written skills</li>
</ul>
<p>For instance, here is a job posting for a data analyst at a New York-based finance company:</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/Picture1-1-3.png" alt="Data Analyst Job Skills"></p>
<p>You now have all the details about the job roles, what functionalities they cater to, and the salary ranges. Time for your final leap –</p>
<h3>Acquiring Requisite Skill Sets</h3>
<p>It is alright if any of the skills are missing from your resume. Not everyone knows everything, but there is always a scope to learn.</p>
<p>You may not have the bandwidth to take a full-fledged degree course to acquire each skill. In fact, you needn’t. The time-saving (and cost-saving) alternative is to look up <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/courses">skill-relevant courses on AnalytixLabs</a> and get yourself enrolled.</p>
<p>These online classes are your key to instant knowledge acquisition because the course contents focus on industrial needs. All the jargon is avoided, and you’ll learn exactly what you require to make an amazing career as a business analyst or data analyst.</p>
<p>Here are a few courses with which you can kickstart your analyst career:</p>
<p><em><strong>For the Data Analyst role in company</strong></em></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/data-science-using-python">Data Science &#x26; Machine Learning with Python</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/business-analytics-data-science-course">Certificate course in Business Analytics</a></li>
</ul>
<p><em><strong>For the Business Analyst role in company</strong></em></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/business-analyst-training-course-online">Analytics Edge</a> (using Excel, SQL, Tableau &#x26; R)</li>
<li><a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/advanced-excel-training-certification-course-online">Data Analytics &#x26; Visualisation</a></li>
</ul>
<p>To understand more about Data Analytics courses and your career prospects, contact the <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/">AnalytixLabs</a> team now!</p>
<p>Hope this answers all your queries… If there is anything more you’d like to know, you can mention it in the comments section. Happy learning!</p>
